hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24292","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Utbah informed us, Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali ibn Shayban al-Suhaymi narrated to us, my father narrated to me: That he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not look at the prayer of a servant who does not straighten his backbone between his bowing and his prostration."
"24293","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Mulazim ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Badr narrated to us, that Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali narrated to him, that his father Ali ibn Shayban narrated to him, that he said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he turned away and saw a man praying alone behind the row. So the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood until the man finished his prayer. So he said to him: Repeat your prayer, for there is no prayer for one alone behind the row."
"24294","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Abu Abdillah al-Shaqari narrated to us, Umar ibn Jabir narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Badr, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ali, from his father, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Allah does not look at a man who does not straighten his backbone in his bowing and in his prostration."
